{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/451397-some-questions-about-the-host-2e","id":451397,"title":"Some questions about the Host, 2e","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-21T04:11:51-07:00","id":451397,"title":"Some questions about the Host, 2e","content":"If a werewolf encounters one, or more, of the Host. Is he guaranteed to recognize them? Is there a reasonable chance he may just think they're a normal critter, provided they're not doing anything special? <br /> <br /> If a werewolf hasn't encountered, or has a good chance of never hearing about the Host - would he recognize them as supernatural? Are they maybe somewhere in between &quot;solid&quot; and &quot;ephemeral&quot;? (in a strange way, like a werewolf is?)<br /> <br /> Do spirits fear / protect / like the Host? Does it depend on the spirit and circumstance? <br /> <br /> If a werewolf chomps up one or many of a Host, does he get some essence? Are the Host essence housing critters?<br /> <br /> I have to thank the discussion on new varieties of the Host, here and in the book. I've made my own Host that I like and I hope will be surprising in game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5220-mother-s-love","name":"Mother's Love","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T04:20:11-07:00","id":451418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mother's Love</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/451397-some-questions-about-the-host-2e#post451397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a werewolf encounters one, or more, of the Host. Is he guaranteed to recognize them? Is there a reasonable chance he may just think they're a normal critter, provided they're not doing anything special?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not guaranteed to recognise them, no, although there are likely to be signs and hints to look for. Hosts tend to act erratically by human standards; the changes they undergo can also lend other tells like strange smells and the sort. Obviously when spiders start crawling out their eyesockets things have gotten pretty obvious.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If a werewolf hasn't encountered, or has a good chance of never hearing about the Host - would he recognize them as supernatural? Are they maybe somewhere in between &quot;solid&quot; and &quot;ephemeral&quot;? (in a strange way, like a werewolf is?) </div> </div> </div>A werewolf who has not encountered a Host won't automatically recognise one as supernatural, no, unless they use the Scent of the Unnatural Facet. Hosts are not made of ephemera.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do spirits fear / protect / like the Host? Does it depend on the spirit and circumstance? </div> </div> </div>Depends on the type of Host, the spirit and the circumstance. No-one likes getting caught in an Azlu's web and having the Essence sucked out of them, or running into a pack of frenzied Beshilu, but there are spirits that work with the Hosts, that fill an ecological niche like parasites or scavengers around the activities of Hosts, and that find Hosts an offence that they kill when they encounter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If a werewolf chomps up one or many of a Host, does he get some essence? Are the Host essence housing critters? </div> </div> </div>Hosts use Essence but werewolves don't get Essence from eating them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have to thank the discussion on new varieties of the Host, here and in the book. I've made my own Host that I like and I hope will be surprising in game. </div> </div> </div>Tell us about your Host! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T14:45:30-07:00","id":452030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/451397-some-questions-about-the-host-2e?p=451418#post451418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tell us about your Host! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I will in time, but I know one player that lurks among these forums. I don't want to provide inadvertent spoilers! I hope to share my idea if it runs well and once the concept is revealed in game. There's that thread about the moth hosts I thought I may post in.<br /> <br /> Thank you for this information - excited for the first Siskur-Dah, which should probably happen tonight. <br /> <br /> In an additional bit of conversation, I really like how after thinking about it a while - I've come to think that perhaps werewolves are a type of the Host themselves. They are part ephemeral and part of flesh, they live in both worlds and travel between them, they frequently gather in large groups and have a profound effect on the gauntlet in the places they inhabit. Maybe they are not of the Host, but maybe the similarities point at the origins of the Host. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5220-mother-s-love","name":"Mother's Love","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"ke